CONSEQUENCE: A public unauthenticated endpoint hands back Notion's error envelope, which carries the database_id (a0fceda5610e474fac5949ec6ab8d012), the Notion request id, and — for a duplicate email — a message that confirms the address is already on the waitlist. Separately, an unbounded `role` string auto-creates Notion select options on write; Notion caps a select at 100 options, so ~100 junk POSTs permanently break every subsequent waitlist write. The remediation was applied to the copy that is NOT in production and never backported to the one that is.

